* SPAN DEMO
* ---------
* SPAN(chars) is a pattern that matches a maximal run of one or more
* characters drawn from the given set. Here we scan TEXT for the first
* run of digits and bind it to N with the . operator.
*   :F(NO)  -- if no digit run is found, branch to NO
* Subject "abc 123 xyz" yields N = "123".
       DIGITS = SPAN('0123456789')
       TEXT = 'abc 123 xyz'
       TEXT DIGITS . N :F(NO)
       OUTPUT = N :(END)
NO     OUTPUT = 'no match'
END
